index 4479b53..d04e1c3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,20 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Browser agent tools
+
+WebMCP-capable browsers can discover tools on every page. Browsers without WebMCP continue to use the same controls. Registration uses `document.modelContext` (with support for the original `navigator.modelContext` preview), and is cleaned up on Astro navigation.
+
+- `open_search` opens the search flyout and exposes its `search_articles` form (`query`). Results match article titles and summaries.
+- `open_reading_list` opens the reading list and exposes its `manage_reading_list` form (`slug`, `action`: `add` or `remove`).
+- `list_articles`, `get_reading_list`, and `set_article_bookmark` (`slug`, boolean `saved`) are available throughout the site. Bookmark updates share the browser session and synchronize visible controls.
+- Article pages expose `read_current_article`. The coastal, coffee, plant, and Super Bowl articles also expose `get_tide_levels`, `get_coffee_brew`, `get_plant_stats`, or `get_article_popularity`, respectively. These return HTTP status, redirect details, and response bodies; the sample API failure scenarios remain in place.
+
+Both forms use `toolname`, `tooldescription`, and `toolautosubmit`, and return their asynchronous results with `SubmitEvent.respondWith` when invoked by an agent. See the [declarative API documentation](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api) and [WebMCP draft](https://webmachinelearning.github.io/webmcp/).
+
+Run client utility and mocked registration/navigation tests with Node 24+:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/browser-tools.test.mjs
+```
